d feasibility are currently unknown.\\\",\\\"effects\\\":\\\"Allow physically supported shaping attempts and inspection of their actual results. Unsuitable material or failed attempts must remain possible. Report evidence sufficient to decide whether an edge can be used by the drying interface, without free mastery, invented measurements, guaranteed success or rewards.\\\"}},\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"guard\\\":null},{\\\"action\\\":{\\\"interface\\\":\\\"rest\\\",\\\"args\\\":{}},\\\"repeat\\\":30,\\\"until\\\":{\\\"path\\\":\\\"self.energy\\\",\\\"comparison\\\":\\\"gte\\\",\\\"value\\\":39},\\\"guard\\\":{\\\"path\\\":\\\"self.energy\\\",\\\"comparison\\\":\\\"lt\\\",\\\"value\\\":39}}],\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"interrupts\\\":[],\\\"notes\\\":[\\\"Thin-slice drying is mastered, but no suitable cutting edge has been established.\\\",\\\"Gathering stone is acquisition, not evidence of its sharpness, hardness or safety.\\\",\\\"Keep the remaining roots carried; do not expose or cut them without meeting the tool prerequisites.\\\"],\\\"projects\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"root-preservation\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can a practical learned method make gathered roots last longer without unacceptable safety or material costs?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"The whole-root trial recorded equal decay gains of 9.2054592 for exposed and carried roots over eight rounds.\\\",\\\"Thin-slice-food-drying-trial was mastered through actual study at tick 28.\\\",\\\"Its contract requires a suitable carried stone or flint edge; no such tool is currently established.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"Local stone suitability, feasible edge manufacture, drying performance and food safety remain unverified.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Conduct a supported comparison of prepared food with an untreated control, without assuming preservation or safety.\\\",\\\"completedSteps\\\":[\\\"Completed and stopped a whole-root exposure comparison.\\\",\\\"Shared its negative preservation result.\\\",\\\"Learned the thin-slice trial.\\\"],\\\"outputs\\\":[\\\"Whole-root exposure comparison: no decay advantage observed.\\\"],\\\"missing\\\":\\\"A physically suitable cutting tool and actual prepared-food trial evidence.\\\",\\\"next\\\":\\\"Acquire stone and seek a paid, learnable edge-making and checking trial.\\\",\\\"pauseReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"benefit\\\":\\\"The negative result avoids treating whole-root exposure as demonstrated preservation; the next prerequisite is explicit.\\\"}],\\\"cares\\\":null,\\\"views\\\":{}}\"}","logprobs":[]}

